JJ) that can carry my weak singles (6, 10), alongside two pairs (99, QQ) and top singles (K, A, RJ). To effectively reduce my hand count using the triplets, I must seize the initiative. Playing the Ace is the optimal move here; it beats the King without wasting the Red Joker (my ultimate control card) and forces the opponents to either pass or spend a 2, which is a favorable trade. Passing would passively allow the Left player (who has 16 cards) to dictate the game, which is dangerous.\n\nReason: The Ace is the most efficient card to beat the King, preserving the Red Joker for emergencies (like a Black Joker or high 2). Gaining the lead is essential to play my triplets with attached singles (333+6, JJJ+10) and advance my game plan.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦A"]}'}
