es or pairs (your highest non-Joker single is K, highest pair is Q). To effectively play these combinations and discard your low kicker cards (6, 10), you absolutely need the initiative.\n\nReason: You need control of the board to play your structural combinations (Triplets 333 and JJJ). If you pass, the opponent may continue to play high cards or clear their hand, and your weak singles (6, 10) will become liabilities. Using the Red Joker to beat the 2 stops the opponent\'s momentum and allows you to transition into playing your Triplets.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["RedJoker"]}'}
